  [1mClassification: architectural.[0m The request names reuse across multiple forms, but only one form exists — there's no
  second consumer to read. So this isn't a tweak to an existing flow; it means introducing a validation module with an
  interface other forms will depend on, and deciding how rules are declared and how errors surface. That's new
  structure, so I'll work through the full process: clarifying questions, 2-3 approaches, a sectioned design, and a
  written spec before any code.

  Also worth flagging: [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is browser-global script-tag code while [38;5;153msrc/[39m uses CommonJS [38;5;153mrequire[39m. Where the shared
  module lives and how both worlds load it is a real decision, not a detail — I'll fold it into the design.

